{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>And its tongs.</b> They are the tongs made to take the wick from within the oil, to set it and to draw it at the mouth of the lamps, and because one takes with them they are called מֶלְקָחַיִם; and צִבְתָהָא, which Onkelos translates, means tongs — טנייל\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>And its ash-pans.</b> They are like small scoops with which one sweeps the ash from the lamp in the morning, when he tends the lamps, from the ash of the wicks that burned through the night and went out; and the term מַחְתָּה is פויישר\"יא בְּלַעַ\"ז, as in ״לַחְתּוֹת אֵשׁ מִיָּקוּד״ (Isaiah 30)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French tenaille(s), 'tongs'", 1 "the la'az is Old French feuillère or foirère, a small pan/shovel for embers or ash"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:36.283578976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}